  <h2 class="bm-h2" id="retro-vs-fluor">Retroreflective vs. fluorescent: a critical distinction</h2>

  <p>One of the most dangerous misconceptions in road-user safety is that "high-visibility yellow" (the bright neon used on construction vests and running gear) keeps you visible after dark. <strong>It does not.</strong> Most road users get this wrong.<sup><a href="#ref-2" class="bm-cite">2</a></sup></p>

